-- title:
--   Descent of an absolutely irreducible two-dimensional representation to a finite field
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a group, $k_0$ a finite field, $F$ a field, $e_0 : k_0 \to F$ a ring homomorphism, and $\rho : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ a group homomorphism. Two hypotheses are imposed. First, for every $x \in G$ and every index $i \in \mathbb{N}$, the $i$-th coefficient of the characteristic polynomial of the underlying matrix of $\rho(x)$ lies in the image of $e_0$. Second, $\rho$ is absolutely irreducible in the following sense: for every field $F'$, every ring homomorphism $e : F \to F'$ and every nonzero vector $u \in (F')^2$, there is some $x \in G$ such that the matrix obtained from $\rho(x)$ by applying $e$ entrywise sends $u$ outside the line $F' \cdot u$; that is, no nonzero vector spans a line stable under all of $\rho(G)$ after any change of field. The conclusion asserts the existence of a group homomorphism $\rho_0 : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(k_0)$ and an element $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ such that, for all $x \in G$, the entrywise image under $e_0$ of the matrix of $\rho_0(x)$ equals $g\,\rho(x)\,g^{-1}$, and such that the matrices $\rho_0(x)$, $x \in G$, span the $k_0$-vector space of all $2 \times 2$ matrices over $k_0$. Finiteness is assumed only of the field of definition $k_0$; the field $F$ is arbitrary.
--
--   This is the two-dimensional case of the descent of an absolutely irreducible representation to the subfield generated by the coefficients of its characteristic polynomials, in the style of Deligne–Serre, strengthened by the assertion that the descended matrices span the full matrix algebra over the small field. It is used in the construction of a conjugate of a two-dimensional Galois representation defined over a finite field, where the spanning clause supplies the surjectivity needed to control stable lines.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Representation_exists_map_eq_conj_and_span_range_eq_top_of_charpoly_coeff_mem_range_of_finite_fin_two.lean

import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.Defs
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Charpoly.Basic
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Span.Defs

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
